==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Otter]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*15 [[Zuche]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Zamelle]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Razorback]] spawns.
**2 [[Prof. Owlbrowley]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Deathshund]] spawns after 25.33 seconds<sup>760f</sup>.
**1 [[Dark Otter]] spawns after 35.33 seconds<sup>1,060f</sup>.
**1 [[Razorback]] spawns after 110 seconds<sup>3,300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A simple stage: perma-Freeze the Dark Otter using [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] while meatshielding with [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]]. This minimizes the damage it takes and lets you completely max out your wallet. Catch the burrowing Zuches with [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCats]], who will instantly kill them. Once you're ready to proceed, send out [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] and start stacking [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cats]] to finish the job. Newtone can be clipped by unburrowing Zuches when making his way to the enemy base, so keep spamming Cadaver BearCats to protect him. Once Razorback appears, he's still countered by [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack Cat]] and Bombercat even with the presence of Prof. Owlbrowley, so you should focus on damaging the backliners instead ([[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]'s [[Wave Attack]]s do a good job at this). Make sure to unburrow Deathshund with [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] too! The [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] here are no joke, but can't push very hard on their own, which means you can stall them out until the second Razorback appears.

Second verse, same as the first, Bombercat and Pizza Cat get it done. You can use [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to nuke him while he's frozen to speed things up, since he poses basically no threat and refunds you when he dies. Cleanup is arguably the most arduous task in this stage, as you have to repeatedly bash your head into the brick wall that is Deathshund twice if you fail to take it out with a [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]]. A fair few Holy Blasts is all you need though.

==Trivia==
*[[wikipedia:Whey protein|Whey]] is a form of protein very commonly found in protein powders and drinks used to provide raw material to build muscle during bodybuilding.
*[[Razorback|Razorback's]] appearance in this stage might be a reference to his enemy unit description where it is stated that he had spent years wandering in wastelands before.

